<Layout chapter="social-program">
  <ChapterHead chapter="social-program" />

  <article class="prose">
    <p>The ICPS we are proposing is designed as a travelling experience, taking you on a journey through some of the most fascinating places our country has to offer. We don't simply want to show you Italy- we want you to experience it through the eyes of those who live here, turning each city into an opportunity to discover its culture, traditions, and the moments that bring people together. The first four days will be spent in <strong>Milano</strong>, the starting point of our journey. During your stay, you will have the opportunity to personalize your experience by choosing the location of a full-day excursion. You can either be captivated by the maritime charm and rich history of <strong>Liguria</strong>, immerse yourself in the breathtaking landscapes and relaxed atmosphere of <strong>Lake Como</strong> or go trekking in the <strong>Lombard Prealps</strong>. <strong>The choice is yours</strong>; which side of Northern Italy would you like to discover?</p>

    <p>The final three days will take us to <strong>Torino</strong>, an elegant city steeped in history, where the social program will end with unique experiences that combine culture, entertainment and local traditions.</p>

    <p>Throughout the week, we will alternate cultural activities, guided tours, team games, themed evenings and plenty of opportunities to socialise. Every experience has been carefully designed not only to help you discover the places we will visit, but above all to connect with the people who will share this adventure with you.</p>

    <p><em>After all, ICPS is much more than a physics conference: it is a place where different cultures meet, friendships are born, and memories are made to last a lifetime</em>.</p>

    <p>To accompany you throughout the journey, we have also prepared a dedicated playlist. Some of the most iconic songs of Italian music will become the soundtrack of your experience, making every stop along the way even more memorable.</p>

    <p>But now... let's take a closer look at everything that awaits you. </p>

    <section>
      <h2>Opening ceremony</h2>

      <p>The opening ceremony of the conference will take place in the prestigious <strong>Courtyard of Ca’ Granda</strong>, part of the historic headquarters of the <strong>Università degli Studi di Milano</strong>. This architectural complex, originally designed as the Ospedale Maggiore in the 15th century, represents one of the most emblematic examples of Renaissance civic architecture in Northern Italy. Today it stands as a symbol of academic excellence and scientific tradition, hosting one of the country’s leading universities.</p>

      <Figure src="social/ca-granda.jpg" alt="Courtyard of Ca' Granda, Università degli Studi di Milano" />

      <p>The Courtyard itself offers a unique setting where historical heritage and academic life coexist, providing an atmosphere of remarkable elegance and cultural significance. Its monumental arcades and harmonious proportions create a distinguished environment that reflects the intellectual identity of the institution and offers an ideal backdrop for welcoming an international community of young researchers in physics.</p>

      <p>The ceremony will begin with a series of <strong>institutional greetings</strong> from representatives of the local organizing committee and invited academic guests. This will be followed by a formal presentation of the conference, including an overview of the scientific program, highlighting its main thematic areas and an introduction to the social program designed for the week. During this session, participants will also be introduced to selected invited speakers and distinguished guests who will contribute to the academic sessions of the conference.</p>

      <p>Following the formal part of the event, a traditional <strong>Italian aperitivo</strong> will be offered to all participants. The reception will provide a relaxed and informal setting aimed at fostering interaction and networking among attendees from different countries and academic backgrounds. The evening is designed to be intentionally light and welcoming, allowing participants to gradually acclimate to the new environment and time zone while remaining a great opportunity to welcome everybody in our community and to get to know each other.</p>

      <p>In case of adverse weather conditions, the ceremony will be relocated to an indoor venue within the same university complex, ensuring full continuity of the program without changes in timing, capacity or format. The backup solution preserves the academic character of the event while guaranteeing a seamless transition between the formal ceremony and the networking aperitivo. </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Excursion day</h2>

      <p>The excursion day is designed to be one of the highlights of the Conference Social Program, offering participants the opportunity to experience the diversity of Northern Italy while simultaneously serving as the <strong>transfer day from Milano to Torino</strong>. Combining the excursion with the relocation between the two host cities allows for a more efficient use of resources, minimizing transportation costs without compromising participants' experience.</p>

      <p>Participants will be <strong>divided into groups</strong> according to their preferences and transported by chartered coaches departing from Milano in the morning and arriving in Torino in the evening. The program has been designed to accommodate both the expected attendance of 400 participants and a possible increase to 500 participants while maintaining a balanced distribution across the proposed destinations.</p>

      <DataTable
        headers={['Destination', 'Scenario A People', 'Scenario A Coaches', 'Scenario B People', 'Scenario B Coaches']}
        rows={[
          ['Genova', 80, 2, 100, 2],
          ['Cinque Terre', 140, 3, 200, 4],
          ['Lake Como', 120, 3, 125, 3],
