        ]}
        foot={['Total', 400, 10, 500, 11]}
      />

      <p>Overall, the excursion day highlights the extraordinary diversity of Northern Italy, from the Mediterranean coastline and UNESCO World Heritage Sites to alpine landscapes, historic monuments and lakeside villages. Beyond sightseeing, the program is intended to foster informal networking, cultural exchange and community building before the conference continues in Torino.</p>

      <h3>Liguria</h3>
      <p>Two of the main destinations of the excursion day are located in Liguria, a seaside region located in the north-western part of Italy well renowned for its stunning coastline and the colorful villages. It is home to the Italian Riviera and attracts visitors from all over the world for its natural beauty and rich culture.</p>

      <Figure src="social/genova.jpg" alt="The harbour and old town of Genova" layout="inset">
        <p><strong>Genova</strong></p>
        <p>One of the historically most important ports in the Mediterranean Sea. It is famous for its old town, its aquarium, the beautiful harbor and the songwriting tradition rooting back to Fabrizio De André.</p>
      </Figure>

      <p>Here participants will have the opportunity to visit the <strong>aquarium of Genova</strong>, one of the largest aquariums in Europe and one of the city's main attractions. Afterwards, they will have free time to explore the UNESCO-listed <strong>historic centre</strong>, wandering through the characteristic <em>vicoli</em> and <em>creuze</em>, discovering elegant squares, medieval architecture and the vibrant old harbour. The combination of maritime history, culture and the relaxed atmosphere of the Italian Riviera makes Genoa an ideal destination for an adventure.</p>

      <Figure src="social/cinque-terre.jpg" alt="The colourful villages of the Cinque Terre" layout="inset">
        <p><strong>Cinque Terre<br />national park</strong></p>
        <p>One of Italy's most renowned UNESCO World Heritage sites, the Cinque Terre National Park is famous worldwide for its five colourful villages perched dramatically on the cliffs overlooking the Mediterranean Sea.</p>
      </Figure>

      <p>Depending on individual preferences, participants may either <strong>explore the villages and panoramic trails</strong> of the National Park or <strong>spend the day relaxing on the beaches</strong> and enjoying these unique views on the Mediterranean sea. The flexibility of this destination makes it suitable for participants with different interests, allowing both a more relaxing or a more adventurous experience, while keeping as a common theme the possibility to visit one of Italy's most iconic landscapes.</p>

      <h3>Lake Como</h3>
      <p>Another important destination of the excursion day is located on the Lake Como, one of the most fascinating lakes in Italy located in the Lombardy region. It is famous for its crystal-clear water, charming villages and stunning mountain scenery.</p>

      <Figure src="social/lake-como.jpg" alt="Lake Como and the town of Colico" layout="inset">
        <p><strong>Colico</strong></p>
        <p>A small town located on the northern shore of Lake Como, is a well-known destination among foreign tourists. It is surrounded on one side by the Italian Alps, while on the other by the waters of the lake.</p>
      </Figure>

      <p>Participants will be free to spend the day according to their preferences, choosing among <strong>lakeside walks</strong>, visits to the historic Forte Montecchio Nord and the Abbey of Piona, swimming, <strong>relaxing by the lake</strong> or <strong>informal recreational activities</strong> organized spontaneously within the group. This option is selected in order to provide a more relaxed experience, aiming to showcase the classical <strong>slow life</strong> associated with Italian culture. Fresh meadows with a view on tall mountains, the possibility to travel on the lake by boat if you wish to, visiting picturesque Italian towns by the coast… Any of these options is easily at hand here.</p>

      <h3>Mountain trekking</h3>
      <p>Another group of participant will head towards the Pre-Alpine region located between Milano and Lake Como, where it will be given the possibility to explore different hiking locations. In particular, two possible routes have been chosen, both easily accessible for participants with different levels of experience. These excursions provide an opportunity to enjoy spectacular mountain scenery, forests and panoramic viewpoints. </p>

      <Figure src="social/pian-dei-resinelli.jpg" alt="The Pian dei Resinelli plateau with the Grigne peaks" layout="inset">
        <p><strong>Pian dei Resinelli</strong></p>
        <p>Mountain plateau located above the Lecco branch of Lake Como, at an altitude of approximately 1,200 metres. It is well renowned among locals for the distinctive limestone peaks of the Grigne mountain range. </p>
      </Figure>

      <p>Participants will be able to admire <strong>breathtaking views</strong> over Lake Como, enjoy fresh, cooler air thanks to the starting altitude and take part in an <strong>easy and accessible walk</strong> through the woods, passing wide meadows that provide the perfect setting for a traditional <strong>Italian picnic lunch</strong>. </p>

      <Figure src="social/canzo.jpg" alt="The woods near Canzo under Lake Como" layout="inset">
        <p><strong>Canzo</strong></p>
        <p>Small town located in the woods under Lake Como. It is a well known hiking spot among local people for the Spirit of the Woods trail and for the geological interest of the area, showing evident glacial activity.</p>
      </Figure>

      <p>The main highlight of the excursion is the <strong>Spirit of the Woods trail</strong>, a woodland path featuring hidden sculptures that create a <strong>fairytale-like</strong> atmosphere reminiscent of a Disney movie. This option has been thought in order to offer a more <strong>adventurous</strong> hiking trail, while remaining accessible to hikers of all skill levels.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Milano treasure hunt</h2>

      <Figure src="social/leonardo.jpg" alt="Leonardo da Vinci trail through Milano" layout="inset">
        <p><strong>Following Leonardo's path</strong></p>
        <p>We offer a <strong>city-wide treasure hunt</strong> on one of the evenings spent in Milano, with the aim of combining a friendly competition with an engaging exploration of the city's <strong>historical and scientific heritage</strong>. Participants will be divided into <strong>small teams</strong> of approximately 10 people and will receive the first riddle at a fixed starting time.</p>
        <p>The activity will unfold as a sequential <strong>puzzle-based challenges</strong> throughout the city. Each correctly solved riddle will reveal a clue leading participants to the next destination using digital maps.</p>
      </Figure>

      <p>Upon reaching each location, teams will scan a hidden QR code to unlock the following physics- or mathematics-based challenge, creating a continuous chain of scientific reasoning, teamwork and urban exploration. The event will <strong>conclude at a predefined final location</strong>, where the last and most challenging puzzle will determine the winning team, which will <strong>receive a prize</strong>.</p>

      <p>A possible route has already been designed to connect several of Milano's <strong>most iconic landmarks</strong> through a walk that is both logistically efficient and thematically coherent. Rather than simply guiding participants through the city's main attractions, the treasure hunt is conceived as a journey inspired by the <strong>life and work of Leonardo da Vinci</strong> during his years in Milano. The selected locations, together with the sequence of puzzles, have been chosen to <strong>highlight different aspects of Leonardo's legacy</strong>, ranging from mechanics and engineering to geometry, optics and artistic genius.</p>

      <p>The timing of the treasure hunt has been planned to ensure that the activity concludes early enough for all participants to comfortably return to their accommodation using public transportation, while still enjoying the unique atmosphere of exploring Milano by night.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>FantaICPS</h2>

      <p>FantaICPS is a fantasy game that has become a long-standing <strong>tradition at AISF national events</strong>. It is inspired by <strong>Fantasanremo</strong>, a fantasy game played during the Sanremo Music Festival that has, in recent years, become an integral part of Italian youth culture. One of the main goals of our social program is to let international participants experience the unique atmosphere and traditions that AISF national events usually offer, and FantaICPS seems like the perfect activity to showcase that.</p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>What is FantaICPS?</strong><br>For FantaICPS, each participant receives a fixed amount of <strong>virtual coins</strong> to build their own fantasy team by including “<strong>Players</strong>”, selected conference participants (typically members of the Organizing Committee, IAPS Executive Committee and Committee Presidents). Each Player has a different value according to their role in the Association, ensuring the creation of balanced teams that include Players with different roles in IAPS. During the conference, Players will <strong>earn bonus points</strong> by completing specific actions or challenges and <strong>lose points</strong> through malus events.</li>
        <li><strong>Chose the rules that will form the FantaICPS Rulebook.</strong><br>Approximately <strong>one month before the beginning of ICPS</strong>, all Players who actively take part in the game can either confirm or decline their participation. Every ICPS Participant will receive access to a <strong>shared document</strong>, where they will be invited to propose ideas for both bonuses and maluses. These can be either general, applying to every Player, or personalized, referring to specific Participants in a fun and light-hearted way. Once the proposal phase is over, a part of the Organizing Committee will review all the suggestions and select the most funny, creative and feasible ones, while giving them an <strong>appropriate Score</strong> according to the difficulty of the bonuses and maluses themself. The chosen bonuses and maluses will then form the official <strong>FantaICPS Rulebook</strong>, which will be public before the beginning of ICPS. Example of bonuses, taken from previous AISF events, may include taking a selfie with one participant from every country or offering some snacks to a participant of your choice, while maluses may include saying the word “FantaICPS” or not attending both scientific or social events.</li>
        <li><strong>Complete additional side-quests to gain points.</strong><br>In addition to bonuses and maluses given to the Players, each FantaICPS Participant will be given some <strong>side quests</strong> that can be completed during the conference. Whenever a Participant completes their quest, they will gain some points depending on the difficulty of the quest itself, that will be added to the total score obtained by the Players in their team. This rule has been made in order to give a challenge not only to Players but also to each participant, in order to give a similar experience to everyone.</li>
        <li><strong>Create your own team.</strong><br>Each ICPS Participant will then be able to create their own team through a <strong>specific platform</strong> before the Opening Ceremony takes place. Although each Team can be formed from a specific pool of ICPS participants, <strong>every participant can still crucially influence the game</strong> by helping Players in their team to score points or by completing their personal Side quests. A <strong>Group of volunteers</strong> is created by the Organizing Committee specifically for evaluating the bonuses or maluses. Every ICPS Participant can <strong>inform this Group</strong> about actions performed by Players that may give them either bonuses or maluses, accompanying testimony with a proof (a photo or a video). At the beginning of every day of the Conference, the total score collected by every Player will be shown to all the participants together with the updated ranking of all the Teams in the competition.</li>
        <li><strong>Win special prices.</strong><br>During the <strong>Closing Ceremony</strong>, the Competition will end and the ICPS participants whose teams obtain the highest amount of points will <strong>receive special prices</strong> according to their placement in the <strong>final ranking</strong>. One important aspect of FantaICPS is that, despite its competitive nature, its main goal is to have fun together; any disputes regarding bonuses, maluses, or scoring will be settled by the Organizing Committee, whose decisions are final.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

